an":null}},"source_text":null,"attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" Returns the result of the `cpuid` instruction for a given `leaf` (`EAX`)"},{"DocComment":" and `sub_leaf` (`ECX`)."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" There are two types of information leaves - basic leaves (with `leaf < 0x8000000`)"},{"DocComment":" and extended leaves (with `leaf >= 0x80000000`). The highest supported basic and"},{"DocComment":" extended leaves can be obtained by calling CPUID with `0` and `0x80000000`,"},{"DocComment":" respectively, and reading the value in the `EAX` register. If the leaf supports"},{"DocComment":" more than one sub-leaf, then the procedure of obtaining the highest supported"},{"DocComment":" sub-leaf, as well as the behavior if a invalid sub-leaf value is passed, depends"},{"DocComment":" on the specific leaf."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" If the `leaf` value is higher than the maximum supported basic or extended leaf"},{"DocComment":" for the processor, this returns the information for the highest supported basic"},{"DocComment":" information leaf (with the passed `sub_leaf` value). If the `leaf` value is less"},{"DocComment":" than or equal to the highest basic or extended leaf value, but the leaf is not"},{"DocComment":" supported on the processor, all zeros are returned."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" The [CPUID Wikipedia page][wiki_cpuid] contains information on how to query which"},{"DocComment":" information using the `EAX` and `ECX` registers, and the interpretation of"},{"DocComment":" the results returned in `EAX`, `EBX`, `ECX`, and `EDX`."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" The references are:"},{"DocComment":" - [Intel 64 and IA-32 Architectures Software Developer's Manual Volume 2:"},{"DocComment":"   Instruction Set Reference, A-Z][intel64_ref]."},{"DocComment":" - [AMD64 Architecture Programmer's Manual, Volume 3: General-Purpose and"},{"DocComment":"   System Instructions][amd64_ref]."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [wiki_cp